  "notes": "The ENA Portal count endpoint is reachable without a login and returns plain integers. I ran 7 of the roughly 60 allowed queries, all for human (tax_eq(9606)) runs with base_count>=1e11 split by first_public date. The model string 'Illumina NovaSeq X' works. I did not run the Ultima, AVITI, 'NovaSeq X Plus' or lower base_count buckets, or the other quarters. Two caveats: first_public is the date data was released, not the date it was sequenced, and ENA is dominated by research and consortium batch deposits that lag sequencing by 6-24 months. So it is a weak proxy for clinical consumables. On this data the 6000 share of >100 Gb human runs shows no decline through 2026. That fits the 'permanent tail' view and does not support 1A. Counts are lumpy, so one large consortium upload can swing a quarter. Two of my queries returned the count as a bare '1391'-style integer and the rest were paraphrased by the fetch tool. I read the counts at face value and did not independently re-verify them.",
